{"title":"1974 IMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Remarks_(added_by_pf02,_October_2025)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Remarks (added by pf02, October 2025)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine all possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/1/3410d6c562c66e2a5b747727086d0057875f0c3f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S = \\frac{a}{a+b+d}+\\frac{b}{a+b+c}+\\frac{c}{b+c+d}+\\frac{d}{a+c+d}\\]\" width=\"398\" height=\"39\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/d/52d9871f0ebe04faa75b50d7055c8a05d08120c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c, d,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" /> are arbitrary positive numbers.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/8/1a8b4160f4b9725f2f8e5f721dea7fb56064feaa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2 = \\frac{a}{a+b}+\\frac{b}{a+b}+\\frac{c}{c+d}+\\frac{d}{c+d} &gt; S &gt; \\frac{a}{a+b+c+d}+\\frac{b}{a+b+c+d}+\\frac{c}{a+b+c+d}+\\frac{d}{a+b+c+d} = 1.\\]\" width=\"811\" height=\"39\" /> We will now prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> can reach any range in between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Choose any positive number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. For some variables such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/c/9dce1d5c52f1b9e3d42136d4bfe3d93ae4fb2310.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k, m, l &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/f/def46767213fac2d1888386bdd8c790d221df3ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k + m + l = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"14\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/8/8d860cd35e3a476041559922536fd43588f890ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = ak$\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/2/a42488141553a9290c6eb7e5ea796fc0f06eb56c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = am$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/4/5245d1eab9fd80957a9b06601bd63cd7ca9c6a1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = al$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />. Plugging this back into the original fraction, we get \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/2/d02f927b132ff7906cdd41d0ee652c659aefdc56.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S = \\frac{a}{a+ak+al}+\\frac{ak}{a+ak+am}+\\frac{am}{ak+am+al}+\\frac{al}{a+am+al} = \\frac{1}{1+k+l}+\\frac{k}{1+k+m}+\\frac{m}{k+m+l}+\\frac{l}{1+m+l}.\\]\" width=\"869\" height=\"39\" />\nThe above equation can be further simplified to \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/a/40af264f51c8a66e53dce3403db722bd4cb64ef9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S = \\frac{1}{2-m}+\\frac{k}{2-l}+m+\\frac{l}{2-k}.\\]\" width=\"260\" height=\"37\" />\nNote that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is a continuous function and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/4/8b4c654d7e6fde0e0ba3926215c31fdc47ca8908.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(m) = m + \\frac{1}{2-m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"153\" height=\"37\" /> is a strictly increasing function. We can now decrease <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" /> to make <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> tend arbitrarily close to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. We see <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/c/61c6825f0411efc68dce93d3084a82168e8e61c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lim_{m\\to1} m + \\frac{1}{2-m} = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"157\" height=\"37\" />, meaning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> can be brought arbitrarily close to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. \nNow, set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/e/2fe1d35766f04d2f16ba519a365678c60bc13a55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = d = x$\" width=\"77\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/6/1461c8535e420b181c9b5ed0c27136d5b8070213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = c = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"73\" height=\"16\" /> for some positive real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/5/32581661cddf01ad30c1e36efe72f99eb0a0adca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" />. Then \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/3/7435942f0f16186649ed600505c64cb21403ece0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S = \\frac{2x}{2x+y} + \\frac{2y}{2y+x} = \\frac{2y^2 + 8xy + 2x^2}{2y^2 + 5xy + 2x^2}.\\]\" width=\"327\" height=\"42\" />\nNotice that if we treat the numerator and denominator each as a quadratic in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, we will get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/1/dd118321d1d121d5fa72235f484d75b3341b9330.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + \\frac{g(x)}{2y^2 + 5xy + 2x^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"160\" height=\"42\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/659a6a2610357101d77dbae8eb9bf0b3100c08fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> has a degree lower than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. This means taking <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/6/9b6de2bada3e9fc9cc0f3cb935c9eb4b6461861c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lim_{y\\to\\infty} 1 + \\frac{g(x)}{2y^2 + 5xy + 2x^2} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"230\" height=\"42\" />, which means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> can be brought arbitrarily close to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, we are done.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/f/57f1406b65f9f2e6a365b7356da731780b42cceb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\]\" />\n</p><p>~Imajinary\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Remarks_.28added_by_pf02.2C_October_2025.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Remarks_(added_by_pf02,_October_2025)\">Remarks (added by pf02, October 2025)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Remarks (added by pf02, October 2025)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>1. Strictly speaking, the solution given above is incomplete.\nIt shows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> can be arbitrarily close to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />,\nbut it does not show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> can take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55bbcea2705336d0f3b7fca0004807c02d11c914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbf{any}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"13\" /> value\nin <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69273482bff8727194f6407e55ac1bfa94d9c555.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />.  This is not difficult to prove, but it is not\nobvious or trivial, so it should be mentioned.\n</p><p>Here is an argument:  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/0/b10d5ee88ffc7d59f9c282b366953fb4fa4051f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> be given by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/c/a7c4abe3e7a0c0b7a70280a364bee98c8f400283.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, b_1, c_1, d_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"91\" height=\"18\" />\nand let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/4/7f4caea56d945d0b6e49701b42ce06e0fb92e663.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> be given by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/e/33e64ac8ab5ecc8582cbff77bfcec2eeee1168fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2, b_2, c_2, d_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"91\" height=\"18\" />.  (Think of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/0/b10d5ee88ffc7d59f9c282b366953fb4fa4051f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />\nclose to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/4/7f4caea56d945d0b6e49701b42ce06e0fb92e663.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> close to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />).  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/6/aa65f993f88ffd976bef38d7c782121e2d9c56ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = (1 - t) a_1 + t a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"151\" height=\"20\" />,\nand similarly for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/3/b935c15651d822aa87116a2c254e1a1ff73de233.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b, c, d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/c/29c4454ef738191b6a1471894e860b7fdf449e37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> be given by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/c/42c06de735d79f0b28c30bcbbcf96e67bb1ca42c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c, d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />.\nClearly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/c/29c4454ef738191b6a1471894e860b7fdf449e37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> is a continuous function of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/e/c3e9cfe97d98005023a8c5c6b1d685b8bdd24558.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(0) = S_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" /> and\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/5/b059f5232842c84cea788e547e29935e55052f3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(1) = S_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" />.  By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Intermediate_Value_Theorem\" title=\"Intermediate Value Theorem\">Intermediate Value Theorem</a> for any\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/d/98dbd851e25b850989667a64e642e094431a1a7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S \\in [S_1, S_2]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"92\" height=\"20\" /> there is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" />, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/0/5b0e0c9f34f2662521654d0e3e23213c99045985.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(t) = S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>2. Motivation for the solution:  Take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/c/42c06de735d79f0b28c30bcbbcf96e67bb1ca42c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c, d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> of the same\nmagnitude, for example <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/e/cde6f6d0dd11e0d4b50795d97b2a0e47af75ed6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = b = c = d = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"143\" height=\"14\" />.  Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8e4aa22dfc9cd6a8da851b481e85595cb3cc752.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = 1.333\\dots\\ .$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"118\" height=\"14\" />\nNow take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/3/3834f0cef2a1f4d8524aa5bc8e3faca298550862.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" /> being of higher magnitude than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/5/645be08e4819218ce9af911a12d44623643dcf77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c, d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" />, for example\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/e/d8ed7e4d42857d91716250ed0a958cfee4faf1fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = b = 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"104\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/7/cd7e742d08ffa6ab822d6f15bbd61001891f0fa0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = d = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"77\" height=\"14\" />.  We get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75e3b0c849c5b048572f4c47c44464e8450a3d18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = 1.001\\dots\\ .$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"118\" height=\"14\" />  And, take\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/b/ecbcc91bf2d4c36979bf0fb29c6e06eadf7e3709.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> of higher magnitude than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/7/f67f4a1dfe3f757a6e0ba16ce1f5c6b3ed25049d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b, d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" />, for example <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/b/58bf6de9852c9b0b9b336749ad0d647f4e50d226.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = c = 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"104\" height=\"14\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/a/ffa70b864b632e646592f07323f381155b0a564a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = d = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"77\" height=\"14\" />.  We get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/a/cda087a93805254c2bf24cb8f295cb26f0ac91be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = 1.997\\dots\\ .$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"118\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Take a few more examples if desired.  This suggests <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/4/1b44a6b0089ee2989b470ab480b3f22723f6e4da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 &lt; S &lt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"81\" height=\"15\" />,\nand that we can get values as close to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> as we want.\n</p><p>3. I will give another solution below.  It is computationally more\ninvolved, but conceptually simpler, and it uses no calculus.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Compute, but group terms to make the computations easier.\nAdd 1st and 3rd terms, 2nd and 4th terms, and group <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/b/ecbcc91bf2d4c36979bf0fb29c6e06eadf7e3709.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />\nand <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/7/f67f4a1dfe3f757a6e0ba16ce1f5c6b3ed25049d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b, d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/e/e3e5d89ce09eaaf271768029cd86803c7e7b3251.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = \\frac{a}{a+b+d} + \\frac{b}{a+b+c} + \\frac{c}{b+c+d} + \\frac{d}{a+c+d} =$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"422\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/a/05a845b29737755d4dcce23d81a2304043ed3d7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2ac + (a + c)(b + d)}{ac + (a + c)(b + d) + (a + c)^2} + \\frac{2bd + (a + c)(b + d)}{bd + (a + c)(b + d) + (b + d)^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"493\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Showing that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/2/a3208337e4761bcca48e0f8d9fc11b1f9f661026.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S &lt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" /> amounts to showing that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/d/0bd19c18915e14b47f6e9c990417644ff363660c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4acbd + 3(ac + bd)(a + c)(b + d) + 2ac(b + d)^2 + 2bd(a + c)^2 + 2(a + c)^2(b + d)^2 + (a + c)(b + d)[(a + c)^2 + (b + d)^2] &lt;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"933\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/5/51555110472a3bd7f85bb80f149c425061a2ba5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2acbd + 2(ac + bd)(a + c)(b + d) + 2ac(b + d)^2 + 2bd(a + c)^2 + 4(a + c)^2(b + d)^2 + 2(a + c)(b + d)[(a + c)^2 + (b + d)^2]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"922\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>This reduces to\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/2/392fa75bebf1be1a335d7a8326ff33fdb310bd9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2acbd - (ac + bd)(a + c)(b + d) + 2(a + c)^2(b + d)^2 + (a + c)(b + d)[(a + c)^2 + (b + d)^2] &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"732\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>This is clearly true because the negative terms cancel with\nparts from the positive terms: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/f/c8fb44dde5699a66fdb2646e329380246922c571.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2acbd$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" /> is cancelled by terms\nfrom <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/d/11d919f112efe0e7bf156e987ce1743dd8a51cf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(a + c)^2(b + d)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/2/d620aef9dd3b626fb8e91b4c9e70cb3d32d26fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-(ac + bd)(a + c)(b + d)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"195\" height=\"20\" /> is\ncancelled by terms from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/8/1486a5311f202a827c20ee3a63e062f7899d44d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a + c)(b + d)[(a + c)^2 + (b + d)^2]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"264\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Showing that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/01913844240a4f5711a87d0c7df1b6357b9eb9c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" /> amounts to showing that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/8/c781b5bda10960c9f11eaefa5f6012dc473866d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4acbd + 3(ac + bd)(a + c)(b + d) + 2ac(b + d)^2 + 2bd(a + c)^2 + 2(a + c)^2(b + d)^2 + (a + c)(b + d)[(a + c)^2 + (b + d)^2] &gt;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"933\" height=\"21\" />the negative terms cancel with\nparts from the positive terms: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/f/c8fb44dde5699a66fdb2646e329380246922c571.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2acbd$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" /> is cancelled by terms\nfrom <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/d/11d919f112efe0e7bf156e987ce1743dd8a51cf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(a + c)^2(b + d)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/2/d620aef9dd3b626fb8e91b4c9e70cb3d32d26fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-(ac + bd)(a + c)(b + d)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"195\" height=\"20\" /> is\ncancelled by terms from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/8/1486a5311f202a827c20ee3a63e062f7899d44d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a + c)(b + d)[(a + c)^2 + (b + d)^2]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"264\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/e/cae5009ea1f6d761717ad902345a83cb90b6d634.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$acbd + (ac + bd)(a + c)(b + d) + ac(b + d)^2 + bd(a + c)^2 + 2(a + c)^2(b + d)^2 + (a + c)(b + d)[(a + c)^2 + (b + d)^2]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"877\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>This reduces to\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/a/b3ae3ad234ef32644166165215583513de524c8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3acbd + 2(ac + bd)(a + c)(b + d) + ac(b + d)^2 + bd(a + c)^2 &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"490\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>This is clearly true because all the terms are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/9/1b98a367e7a3b900016ce23ba8ecaa33ce029c6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Now show that any number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366c59b4a196f7ea868e8b4b4cddf44453223b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S \\in (1, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" /> is the result of the sum\nof the fractions in the statement of the problem for some\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/c/42c06de735d79f0b28c30bcbbcf96e67bb1ca42c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c, d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />.  First, look for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/1/91133a3ae7cf2784f36bd4bbc812f27be056f8c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = c, b = d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"18\" /> which would yield\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />.  We are looking for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/3/3834f0cef2a1f4d8524aa5bc8e3faca298550862.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" /> such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/0/2008ca6728b1993f937abc32d5f62fd3bcba19c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = \\frac{2a}{a + 2b} + \\frac{2b}{2a + b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"166\" height=\"41\" />.  After some easy\ncomputations this becomes\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/9/789b926614a5290ca2953c2d651633343563e1e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4 - 2S)\\left(\\frac{a}{b}\\right)^2 - (5S - 4)\\left(\\frac{a}{b}\\right) + (4 - 2S) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"363\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>This yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/9/b89e83f1659b65760f8cd85d3255fd20f5a2cb96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{b} = \\frac{5S - 4 \\pm \\sqrt{9S^2 + 24S - 48}}{4 - 2S}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"255\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p>Remembering that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/8/f383a25cbaf4e6cdd01c91d221acbe0da42cf772.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" />, we see that we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/4/084079bf1d54500f3c59257a7ec3467932b72ba2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"34\" /> real and\npositive when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/c/b1c5d480e5c6e33bb9216c4ef2eb70a9e6327417.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S \\in \\left[\\frac{4}{3}, 2\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"89\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p>Now, look for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/7/49727d7b9bf09003fdb2e0ffb47f3de2d2b94b9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = b, c = d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"18\" /> which would yield\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />.  We are looking for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/b/ecbcc91bf2d4c36979bf0fb29c6e06eadf7e3709.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/9/a79ee0f382375bfe6a56ca9a486f5f3d0789702e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = \\frac{2a}{2a + c} + \\frac{2c}{a + 2c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"166\" height=\"40\" />.  After some easy\ncomputations this becomes\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/8/8c883af04ddafa74c2849aac863a41ebf42ef3d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2S - 2)\\left(\\frac{a}{c}\\right)^2 - (8 - 5S)\\left(\\frac{a}{c}\\right) + (2S - 2) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"363\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>This yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/e/22ed1419ba93beb97b7823c320809b0063d9d2ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{c} = \\frac{8 - 5S \\pm \\sqrt{9S^2 - 48S + 48}}{4S - 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"255\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p>Remembering that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/8/f383a25cbaf4e6cdd01c91d221acbe0da42cf772.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" />, we see that we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/6/8362dd17da7c07cedd4018d589a0b21e9575e287.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"12\" height=\"33\" /> real and\npositive when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/f/30f82ccd3031be90b4d1c389ffc09797059ad57c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S \\in \\left(1, \\frac{4}{3}\\right]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"89\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366c59b4a196f7ea868e8b4b4cddf44453223b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S \\in (1, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" /> is the result of the sum of the fractions in the\nstatement of the problem for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/c/42c06de735d79f0b28c30bcbbcf96e67bb1ca42c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c, d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>[Solution by pf02, October 2025]\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_IMO\" title=\"1974 IMO\">1974 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1974 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1974 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1974 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1974 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1974 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1974 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1974 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1974 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017154932\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.050 seconds\nReal time usage: 1.414 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 548/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 895/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 22708/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.397      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    7.397      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:12095:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017154932 and revision id 263133. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}